<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil raises posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil raises posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it raised the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$5.00/cubic metre or C$0.79/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$214.00/cubic metre, or C$34.02/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$210.00/cubic metre, or C$33.39/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$190.00/cubic metre, or C$30.21/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$200.00/cubic metre, or C$31.80/barrel</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
